<section class="mb-5">
  <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
      <h2 class="h1 mb-3">Sand Point Way can be better</h2>
      <div class="d-flex flex-row">
        <div class="flex-grow-1">
          <p class="lead">
            Sand Point Way NE runs through Northeast Seattle, connecting the University
            District to Lake City and major parks such as Magnuson Park and Matthews Beach. 
            For decades it was designated as State Route 513, prioritizing motor vehicle movement.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Though it is no longer a state highway north of Magnuson Park, the corridor is still centered around vehicles.
            This community initiative advocates for changes that will make it more welcoming to other users, like safer crossings and pedestrian-friendly streetscaping.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="crosswalk-image d-flex align-items-start">
          <img src="/assets/xwalk.png" class="img-fluid p-2" alt="crosswalk sign" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved/">Get involved</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/about/">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row g-4 mb-5">
  <div class="col-md-12">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">The problem</h2>
        <p class="card-text">
          Sand Point Way NE has long gaps without safe crossings, minimal or absent sidewalks, and fast-moving vehicles, creating hazardous conditions for pedestrians and cyclists.  Key nearby locations &mdash; Magnuson Park, Burke-Gilman Trail, and surrounding neighborhoods &mdash; lack adequate connectivity, and even walking to the bus stop uis a perilous journey.
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          Along the <strong>three mile stretch</strong> from north Magnuson Park to the intersection at 35th Ave NE, there are <strong>no traffic lights,</strong> encouraging vehicles to drive far above the 25mph limit.  There are <strong>over ten road shoulder configurations</strong> along Sand Point Way through this stretch.  Road safety infrastructure on this corridor road remains lacking, leaving families with limited ways to safely cross this de facto highway.
        </p>
        <p class="card-text mb-0 d-flex justify-content-center">
          <img class="img-fluid" src="/assets/sandpoint.png">
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-12">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">Why now</h2>
        <p class="card-text">
          In 2025 over 220 people suffered severe, life-altering injuries on Seattle streets, with roughly a third of those victims being pedestrians. We don't want to wait for more deaths on Sand Point Way before SDOT takes action. We're calling on the city to fix this arterial so that cars, pedestrians, and other users of the road can all travel and cross safely. 
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          <div>It can be difficult to access Magnuson Park using NE 77th, where no sidewalks exist.</div>
          <img class="w-75 mt-2 mb-4" src="/assets/77th.jpg">
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          <div>The crosswalk at 77th has signage, but the road curve hides people waiting to cross westward, problematic with vehicles commonly traveling over the speed limit.</div>
          <div class="w-75 mt-2 mb-4">
            <div style="position:relative; width:100%; height:0px; padding-bottom:56.250%"><iframe allow="fullscreen;autoplay" allowfullscreen height="100%" src="https://streamable.com/e/4pwteo?autoplay=1&muted=1" width="100%" style="border:none; width:100%; height:100%; position:absolute; left:0px; top:0px; overflow:hidden;"></iframe></div>
          </div>
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          <div>The paved connection from the trail has no clear path across the street to access Magnuson Park.</div>
          <img class="w-75 mt-2 mb-4" src="/assets/bg-conn.jpg">
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          It can also be difficult to access Matthews Beach, without first entering from the Burke-Gilman Trail.
          <img class="w-75 mt-2 mb-4" src="/assets/matthewsbeach.jpg">
        </p>
        <p class="card-text">
          The crosswalk at 95th is well anointed, but there isn't a lot of walking space once you arrive on the east side, which is the only side that has a cutout for crossing under the Burke-Gilman to access Matthews Beach.
          <img class="w-75 mt-2 mb-4" src="/assets/95th.jpg">
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-5">
  <h2 class="h3 mb-3">Our vision</h2>
  <p>We believe that a road that once moved state highway traffic can be redesigned to move people on foot, on wheels, and in transit while remaining an arterial for cars.</p>
  <div class="list-group shadow-sm">
    <div class="list-group-item">Protected pedestrian crossings at major intersections</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Seattle-approved minimum width of sidewalks or protected walkways</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">ADA accessible ramp up to the Burke-Gilman Trail from the 95th St. intersection</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Marked crossing connecting the Burke-Gilman Trail to Magnuson Park</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Dedicated Metro Route 75 bus stops</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Installation of the approved anti-street racing automated traffic camera</div>
  </div>
</section>

